msgid "yes — the identity provider is the invitation"
msgstr "jah – identiteedipakkuja ongi kutse"

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: a person may have a picture of the whole page kept, sent by their browser extension or drawn here from the kept source with scripts and the network off. A picture taken in somebody's browser shows the page as they were seeing it, signed in or not. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep one."
msgstr "Jah: inimene võib lasta säilitada pildi kogu lehest, mille saatis tema brauserilaiendus või mis renderdati siin säilitatud allikast, skriptid ja võrk välja lülitatud. Kellegi brauseris tehtud pilt näitab lehte nii, nagu ta seda nägi, sisse logituna või mitte. Ei või seadmata: kellegi jäädvustused seda ei säilita."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: a person may have the page's source kept beside what was read from it, exactly as it was parsed, so that a capture can be checked against it and read again by a better parser. It is kept as text and never shown as a page. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep it, whatever they have chosen."
msgstr "Jah: inimene võib lasta lehe allika säilitada sellest loetu kõrval, täpselt nii, nagu see parsiti, et jäädvustust saaks sellega võrrelda ja parem parser saaks selle uuesti lugeda. Seda säilitatakse tekstina ja ei näidata kunagi lehena. Ei või seadmata: kellegi jäädvustused seda ei säilita, olenemata nende valikust."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: anyone who finds the address may create an account. No: invitation only. An empty instance always offers the sign-up form, so somebody can become the first account."
msgstr "Jah: igaüks, kes aadressi leiab, tohib konto luua. Ei: ainult kutsega. Tühi Postulo pakub alati registreerimisvormi, et keegi saaks luua esimese konto."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: somebody who arrives through the identity provider is signed straight in, without being asked for a code as well. Say yes only if you know that provider checks identity at least as carefully as Postulo would. It never applies to a password sign-in, and it removes nobody's authenticator app. A passkey already counts on its own and needs no setting."
msgstr "Jah: kes tuleb identiteedipakkuja kaudu, logitakse otse sisse, ilma et küsitaks ka koodi. Vastake jah üksnes siis, kui teate, et see pakkuja kontrollib isikusamasust vähemalt sama hoolikalt kui Postulo. See ei kehti kunagi parooliga sisselogimise kohta ega eemalda kelleltki autentimisrakendust. Pääsuvõti loeb juba iseseisvalt ega vaja seadet."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: somebody who has forgotten their password can ask for a code at their primary address and type it back. A code rather than a link, because mail scanners follow links and would spend one before the person read it. It is never a second factor: an authenticator app is still asked for. Offered only while this instance's mail is actually getting through."
msgstr "Jah: kes on oma parooli unustanud, saab küsida koodi oma põhiaadressile ja selle tagasi sisestada. Kood, mitte link, sest postiskannerid avavad linke ja kulutaksid selle ära enne, kui inimene kirja loeb. See ei ole kunagi teine tegur: autentimisrakendust küsitakse ikkagi. Pakutakse ainult seni, kuni selle Postulo kirjad tegelikult kohale jõuavad."

